title: Microsoft Hyper-V Cluster: CSV I/O
agents: windows
catalog: os/storage
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors the throughput, operations, latency and queue lengths
 of the cluster shared volumes (CSV) as seen from the monitored node, and shows
 whether the node owns the volume. The agent plug-in measures the counters
 over one second.

 Levels are configured with the rule "Disk I/O levels".

 The check is {UNKNOWN} if the agent reports the volume without any counters.

 The data is collected by the agent plug-in {hyperv_host_csv_io.ps1}, which can
 be deployed with the agent bakery rule "Hyper-V".

item:
 The name of the cluster shared volume.

discovery:
 One service is created for each cluster shared volume the node reports.
 The service stays the same when the volume moves to another node.
